  "note": "Builder kit catalogue (Latch, graybox stage). street: one entry per export street-item kind (`kind/variant` wins over `kind`); each part is a Prim in the item's own frame, in fractions of the item size [a along yaw, b across, h] (by: 'h' = every fraction of h, for crowns and heads that outgrow the footprint). c = [along, across], base = fraction of h above the item's z; surface absent = the item's own surface; yaw = extra radians. An export kind missing here is rejected. connectors: surface per kind; vertical ones (foot = head) are shafts on their ring, inclined ones a sloped slab `slab` m thick. crossings: see its own note. batchTile: metres per side of the square tiles meshes are combined into, per layer and material. fadeCell (Latch, 008 B6): the layers the architecture fade may thin are cut further into cells this many metres a side inside their tile (renderer `mat@tx,tz#cx,cz`), so the fade's discarding variant reaches only the cells round the cut, not a whole 64 m tile (Redline item 9); 0 = tiles only. shadowProxies (008 B6, fix 2): kit facades and street trees cast from a LOD1 proxy; held off until the Air shows a gain and Vela and Glint judge it (the proxies are built either way and the perf harness switches them). Forma and Vela tune shapes; Glint and Vela own colour (surfaces are look.json keys).",
